{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"be9df5d2-8869-4e99-bfbc-762417aec977","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A string fixed at both ends can vibrate in three loops. This curve shows one instant, not the path of the string.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Standing waves on a string"},{"op":"figure","id":"string","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.5,6.5],"y":[-1.7,1.7],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"rest","from":[0,0],"to":[6,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"fn","id":"snapshot","y":"sin(pi*x/2)","domain":[0,6]},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,-0.35],"to":[0,0.35]},{"kind":"segment","from":[6,-0.35],"to":[6,0.35]}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"be9df5d2-8869-4e99-bfbc-762417aec977","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Nodes never move. Both fixed ends are nodes, and two more nodes divide this standing wave into three loops.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"nodes","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"node0","at":[0,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"node2","at":[2,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"node4","at":[4,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"node6","at":[6,0],"label":"N"}]},{"op":"text","id":"node_note","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Nodes: always at rest"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"be9df5d2-8869-4e99-bfbc-762417aec977","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Antinodes have the greatest vibration amplitude. The dashed curve shows the opposite extreme; nodes stay fixed while each loop reverses.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"antinodes","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"opposite","y":"-sin(pi*x/2)","domain":[0,6],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","id":"anti1","at":{"on":"snapshot","x":1},"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"anti3","at":{"on":"snapshot","x":3},"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"anti5","at":{"on":"snapshot","x":5},"label":"A"}]},{"op":"text","id":"anti_note","anchor":{"el":"node_note","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Antinodes: greatest amplitude"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What lies halfway between two adjacent nodes?","expected_gist":"An antinode, where vibration amplitude is greatest."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"be9df5d2-8869-4e99-bfbc-762417aec977","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Adjacent nodes are half a wavelength apart. Each loop spans half a wavelength, so this three-loop string has length three halves of a wavelength.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"spacing","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-1.4],"to":[2,-1.4],"label":"λ/2"},{"kind":"measure","from":[1,1.4],"to":[5,1.4],"label":"λ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"length_rule","anchor":{"el":"anti_note","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"L=3\\left(\\frac{\\lambda}{2}\\right)\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\\lambda=\\frac{2L}{3}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
